---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";
import BackLink from "../components/BackLink.astro";
---

<Base title={`Privacy | ${site.name}`} >
  <BackLink />
  <h1 class="mt-1 font-display text-[44px] leading-none font-bold">Privacy</h1>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold">Who is responsible</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">{site.imprint.name}, {site.imprint.street}, {site.imprint.city}. Contact: {site.contactEmail}</p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold">Visiting this site</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    This site is hosted by Vercel Inc. (USA). When you open a page, Vercel's servers record technical data such as your IP
    address, the time and the page requested, to deliver the site and keep it secure. Until you play a video, this site sets no
    cookies and loads no external fonts or scripts (see Videos).
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold">Visitor statistics</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    We use Vercel Web Analytics to count visits: which pages are viewed, the referring site, country, device type and
    browser. It works without cookies and stores no personal profiles; visitors are told apart only by an anonymous
    hash of the request that is reset every day, so visits cannot be linked across days or sites. We cannot see who you
    are.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold">Videos</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    Each drill shows a video from YouTube (Google) that plays right on the page. Nothing is loaded from YouTube until you
    tap it. When you tap, the player loads from youtube-nocookie.com: Google (USA, under the EU-US Data Privacy
    Framework) receives your IP address and device data, may store data in your browser while the video plays, and may
    show ads. If your browser has JavaScript switched off, the tap opens the video on YouTube instead, where YouTube's
    privacy policy applies.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold">Feedback form</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    The feedback link opens a form at Tally (Tally BV, Belgium). Data goes to Tally only if you click that link. The form
    records which session you played and your answers; your email address is optional. Answers are stored at Tally and in
    a Google Sheet (Google) that only the organisers can read, and are used only to improve the sessions.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-6 font-head text-xl font-bold">Your rights</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">
    You can ask us what we store about you, and have it corrected or deleted, by writing to {site.contactEmail}. You can
    also complain to a data protection authority, in Berlin the Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und
    Informationsfreiheit.
  </p>
</Base>
